{"availability":"available","full":"smartcomputer-ai/lightspeed","name":"lightspeed","description":"Deterministic agent harness for Temporal (in Rust)","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":243,"forks":23,"created":"2026-02-09T09:09:53Z","updated":"2026-10-04T07:44:27Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ls.bot/","topics":["agent","agent-harness","ai","autonomous-agents","event-sourcing","rust-lang","software-factory","temporal"],"demo":"https://ls.bot/demo","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:12.116Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:12.116Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:12.116Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:11:12.116Z","stars":243,"forks":23}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Lightspeed is open-source infrastructure for running managed agent fleets as durable workflows.","\"Managed agents\" is an emerging pattern that separates the core agent loops from the VM or sandbox they use. Agents survive restarts, can run for months, and stay cheap when idle. When they need an operating system, they borrow a real machine for as long as the task requires.","Lightspeed's Rust core runs on Temporal today and stores production data in Postgres with optional S3. The frontend is TypeScript and React."],"features":["Personal assistants for thousands of users without one idle VM per user","Autonomous software factories that coordinate agents to build, test, and","On-call operations agents that investigate alerts, propose fixes, and","Research agents that spin up compute for long-running experiments, stay live for days, and supervise progress","[x] OpenAI and Anthropic: support for reasoning, compaction, tools,"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/smartcomputer-ai/lightspeed/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3318e2aa3da054b9ac7d015b01e08372ce64ebff2eeb67e7651cf46fb30a77de","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:12.222Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:12.222Z","pro